# probes register — the ratified drift-gate probes (rung 2 of the unified probe census,
# discover::probes). Every probe here leans only on the SHARED `spec-lock drift gate`
# fire-drill (a tampered or missing committed lock is caught) and has NO individual
# refutation drill of its own. Writing a line IS the ratification; the reason is the one
# thing no derivation produces. Held by set difference against the live drift-gate set
# (`every_probe_has_an_individual_drill_or_is_ratified`): an un-ratified byte-lock refuses,
# and a line for a probe that earned an individual drill is stale — so this set can only
# shrink. To remove a line, give that probe its own drill.
#
# Format: <probe key>: <why it leans on the shared drift gate rather than an individual drill>

surface: the public-surface census (qualify.spec) is derived by boundary-enforce over the source tree; its DERIVATION is mutation-tested in that crate, but no in-crate fire-drill plants a surface that changed without a re-bless. An individual drill would run the census over a synthetic tree with an added public item and demand the line appears.
tiers: the derived tier partition (tiers.spec) is derived by boundary-enforce; its derivation is mutation-tested there, but no in-crate fire-drill plants a mis-derived partition. An individual drill would run derive_partition over a synthetic file that should change tier and demand the move.
reasons: the qualify-reason census (qualify-reasons.spec) is derived by boundary-enforce in the same walk as the surface census; its classifier is unit-probed there (each blocker class has a fixture that produces it, and a qualifying file produces none), but no in-crate fire-drill plants a file whose classes should move and demands the line change. An individual drill would run the classifier over a synthetic tree with a de-primitivised signature and demand the class disappears.
